  "analysis": "Attempt2 data itself was clean (50/50, writes/trace/terminal all 0, 49 success + 1 genuine AGENT_DEADLINE_EXCEEDED on a multi-turn 600519 follow-up under remote-DB latency variance). The rollback was triggered by two runner semantics carried over from P1.8 that contradict the P1.9 spec: (a) ratio gates were enforced per 50-sample window while P1.9 mandates them on the combined >=100 cumulative sample; (b) a no-output Pi deadline was counted as safety-incorrect although safety_correctness measures unsafe output (fabrication/wrong doc) — deadlines are reliability events tracked by unexpected_timeout. Both corrected; the observed deadline still counts toward the combined ratio budget."
